Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.43,0:00:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,To change a qubit's state we use operations called\Nquantum gates The X gate swaps the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.26,0:00:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,zero and one states The Hadamard gate represented by the\Nletter H transforms a zero into
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.73,0:00:15.06,Default,,0,0,0,,a superposition with equal probabilities in the\Nmeasurement basis Other gates change the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.07,0:00:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,phase or perform rotations We can draw these operations\Nalong a line first prepare the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.76,0:00:25.05,Default,,0,0,0,,state then apply the gates and finally measure This\Ndrawing is a quantum circuit The
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.06,0:00:30.11,Default,,0,0,0,,order of operations matters As with a recipe changing\Nthe steps can change the result and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.12,0:00:33.15,Default,,0,0,0,,a single operation does not explain the behavior of the\Nentire circuit